\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Algebraic singlets and the finite connection law}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [dressed pair](fdip-00WD), the integral
exterior singlet of \ref{fdip-00WX}, and the modular
area singlet of \ref{fdip-00X1} are specified elements
or families in finite exterior algebras.
Gauge invariance describes their transformation
law. It does not by itself assign a physical
hadron, a statistics interpretation, or a
continuum particle to any of them.}

\p{For the rational sign example, extension to
#{\mathbb R} and the positivity result of
\ref{fdip-00U7} give the probability law on
connections described in \ref{fdip-00TX}.
The matter insertion still uses the signed
[Berezin coefficient](fdip-00TJ).
Its conditional inverse-kernel formula and its
global connection average are distinct operations.}
